    week: 4,
    foodFocus: "Your gut does a lot more than simply digest food, but looking after it does not require an extreme diet or a cupboard full of special products. This week we are focusing on the basics that matter: eating a varied diet, getting enough fibre from normal foods, including different vegetables, fruit, legumes, grains, nuts and seeds across the week, drinking enough fluid, and paying attention to how your own digestive system responds. More fibre is not automatically better overnight. If your usual intake is fairly low, suddenly adding large amounts of beans, bran, seeds and raw vegetables can leave you feeling uncomfortable. Build variety gradually and use cooked vegetables, smaller portions of legumes and simpler meals when that suits your digestion better. Fermented foods can be part of a healthy diet if you enjoy and tolerate them, but they are not compulsory and they are not a treatment for every gut symptom. The aim this week is not to create the “perfect microbiome”. It is to build a way of eating that gives your digestive system regular exposure to a broad range of normal foods while still feeling comfortable and achievable.",
